	// DecideDeviceCodeWithResponse Approve or deny a device sign-in as the signed-in user.
	//
	// What the console's `/device` page sends once the person reads the code their CLI printed (ADR-0120). Approving signs that CLI in as this user, so the page says what is being approved: anyone who gets a person to approve a code they did not start signs a CLI in as them. A code no live, undecided authorization holds answers 404, whether it was never issued, has lapsed or is decided. The code is read without case, separator or surrounding space.
